{"abstract":[{"text":"Detect active screen capture sessions and respond appropriately to protect sensitive content in your app.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/technologies","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI","doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/View-configuration"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.SwiftUI\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/Protecting-sensitive-content-when-screen-sharing"},"kind":"article","legalNotices":{"copyright":"Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.","privacyPolicy":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/privacy\/privacy-policy","termsOfUse":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/legal\/internet-services\/terms\/site.html"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftUI"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Protecting sensitive content when screen sharing and remote control are active"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Screen sharing and remote control features offer people useful ways to collaborate. As screen sharing becomes more common, apps that handle sensitive data — such as banking, payments, and healthcare apps — should take steps to protect content during active capture sessions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS and iPadOS provide a built-in API to detect when the system captures a scene. Respond to this signal and take proactive steps in your app to protect sensitive content during any capture session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Detect-when-the-system-captures-your-apps-content","level":2,"text":"Detect when the system captures your app’s content","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a screen capture session is active — including screen recording, mirroring, or remote control — the system updates the scene’s capture state. Use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/SwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/isSceneCaptured","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"isSceneCaptured","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"isSceneCaptured","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"reference"},{"text":" environment value in SwiftUI or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/UIKit\/UITraitCollection\/sceneCaptureState","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"UITraitCollection.sceneCaptureState","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"UITraitCollection.sceneCaptureState","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"reference"},{"text":" in UIKit to observe this state. When the state changes, update your UI accordingly — for example, replacing sensitive views with redacted or placeholder content.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"tabs":[{"content":[{"code":["struct AccountView: View {","    @Environment(\\.isSceneCaptured) private var isSceneCaptured","","    var body: some View {","        if isSceneCaptured {","            \/\/ Replace `RedactedContentView` with your redacted or placeholder view.","            RedactedContentView()","        } else {","            \/\/ Replace `SensitiveContentView` with your content view.","            SensitiveContentView()","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"title":"SwiftUI"},{"content":[{"code":["override func viewDidLoad() {","    super.viewDidLoad()","    \/\/ Register to observe scene capture state changes.","    registerForTraitChanges([UITraitSceneCaptureState.self]) { (self: Self, previousTraitCollection: UITraitCollection) in","        self.updateContentVisibility()","    }","    \/\/ Apply the initial state on load.","    updateContentVisibility()","}","","func updateContentVisibility() {","    let isCaptured = traitCollection.sceneCaptureState != .notCaptured","    \/\/ Replace `accountNumberLabel` and `balanceLabel` with the sensitive UI elements you want to hide.","    accountNumberLabel.isHidden = isCaptured","    balanceLabel.isHidden = isCaptured","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"title":"UIKit"}],"type":"tabNavigator"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"sceneCaptureState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t differentiate between capture types. Screen recording, AirPlay mirroring, and remote control all produce the same signal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Respond-to-capture-sessions","level":2,"text":"Respond to capture sessions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The right response depends on the sensitivity of the data your app handles and the potential impact to people if that content is exposed during a capture session. An app that displays financial account details or personal health information may warrant stronger protections than a general-purpose app. Assess the appropriate level of protection for people using your app to determine how to respond when your app detects a capture session:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Inform the person.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Display a banner or in-app notification letting people know their screen is being shared.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hide or redact sensitive fields.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Replace account numbers, balances, card details, and passwords with placeholder text or a blur overlay. The Passwords app uses a similar pattern to protect sensitive content from screenshots.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Disable high-risk actions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Prevent fund transfers, password reveals, or other irreversible operations from completing while capture is active.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Balance-protection-with-usability","level":2,"text":"Balance protection with usability","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/UIKit\/UITraitCollection\/sceneCaptureState","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"UITraitCollection.sceneCaptureState","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"UITraitCollection.sceneCaptureState","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"reference"},{"text":" activates for all capture events, including everyday uses like recording a tutorial or mirroring to a personal Apple TV. Keep these considerations in mind when deciding how to respond:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apply protections selectively.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Target the highest-risk areas of your app rather than blocking functionality broadly. A blanket app-level lockdown may frustrate people with legitimate screen-sharing needs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use neutral language.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Avoid messaging that implies the person is under attack. A calm, informative notification — such as “Screen sharing is active. Some content is protected during this session.” — is less alarming and more effective.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Weigh the tradeoff for your audience.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A banking app with stricter security requirements may justify more restrictive behavior than a general-purpose app. Design your response based on your app’s specific risk profile.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Redacting-private-content","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/wa